            <ArticleTitle>Prevalence of back pain among radiation therapists.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>460-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Low back pain among radiation therapists appears to be positively associated with age, time working as a radiation therapist and a number of other factors including level of fitness and perceived stress levels. These are the authors' findings from a pilot survey they conducted of radiation therapists employed in eight radiation oncology departments.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
